## 📋 Implementation Plan — Phased Execution

### PHASE 0 — Security & Multi-Tenant Hardening
- Add `@PreAuthorize` to uncovered high-risk controllers (Transactions, Memberships, Analytics, PT Sessions, Member Progress, etc.)
- Enforce gym scoping: propagate `activeGymId` from JWT/session; require `gymId` on all attendance queries
- Add request validation for date ranges and pagination params
- Introduce audit logging for attendance actions (who performed manual check-in/out)

### PHASE 1 — Database & Model Fixes
- Refactor `CheckIn` to use enums:
  - Replace `status: String` with `CheckInStatus { ACTIVE, CHECKED_OUT }`
  - Add `checkInMethod: CheckInMethod { MANUAL, QR, SELF, CLASS }`
- Add audit fields: `deviceInfo`, `ipAddress`, `operatorUserId` (nullable)
- Add `notes` field (optional)
- Fix `gymId` mapping: choose a single source of truth
  - Option A: keep `Long gymId` + `@ManyToOne Gym` with `insertable=true, updatable=true` on `gym` only
  - Option B: keep `Long gymId` (authoritative) and map `@ManyToOne` as read-only association
- Migration (Oracle):
  - `ALTER TABLE CHECK_INS ADD check_in_method VARCHAR2(20) DEFAULT 'MANUAL' NOT NULL;`
  - `ALTER TABLE CHECK_INS ADD status VARCHAR2(20) DEFAULT 'ACTIVE' NOT NULL;` (with backfill)
  - `ALTER TABLE CHECK_INS ADD device_info VARCHAR2(200);`
  - `ALTER TABLE CHECK_INS ADD ip_address VARCHAR2(64);`
  - `ALTER TABLE CHECK_INS ADD operator_user_id NUMBER;`
  - `ALTER TABLE CHECK_INS ADD notes VARCHAR2(500);`

### PHASE 2 — Service Layer (Extract Business Logic)
Create `AttendanceService.java` with:
- `validateAndCheckIn(userId, gymId, method, ctx)` — duplicate prevention + audit
- `checkOut(checkInId, userId, ctx)` — ownership/role validation
- `getTodayAttendance(gymId, role, page)` — gym-scoped, paginated
- `getStats(gymId, role)` — no simulation; real zeros when empty
- `getTrends(gymId, from, to, role)` — real data only
- `getHeatmap(gymId, weeks, role)` — real data only
- `getMemberHistory(userId, from, to)` — self-scope
- `getTrainerMembersAttendance(trainerId, from, to)` — assigned only
- `computeStreak(userId)` — consecutive days visited

### PHASE 3 — Controller Refactor
- Remove `simulateAttendance()` and `simulateHourlyAttendance()` and all fallback usage
- Add/fix endpoints (gym-scoped; paginated where relevant):
  - `GET  /api/attendance/today`
  - `GET  /api/attendance/live`
  - `GET  /api/attendance/stats`
  - `GET  /api/attendance/trends`
  - `GET  /api/attendance/heatmap`
  - `POST /api/attendance/check-in`
  - `PUT  /api/attendance/check-out/{id}`
- Role-specific endpoints:
  - MEMBER: `POST /api/attendance/me/check-in`, `GET /api/attendance/me/history`, `GET /api/attendance/me/streak`
  - TRAINER: `GET /api/attendance/trainer/members` (assigned only)
- Deprecate check-in/out in `DashboardController`; migrate frontend to Attendance endpoints

### PHASE 4 — Frontend Service Update (`attendanceTaskApi.ts`)
- Swap `checkIn()` to `POST /api/attendance/check-in`
- Swap `checkOut()` to `PUT /api/attendance/check-out/{id}`
- Add:
  - `selfCheckIn()` → `POST /api/attendance/me/check-in`
  - `getMyHistory(from, to)` → `GET /api/attendance/me/history`
  - `getMyStreak()` → `GET /api/attendance/me/streak`
  - `getTrainerMembersAttendance(from, to)` → `GET /api/attendance/trainer/members`
- Add pagination params to read endpoints (`page`, `size`)
- Add TypeScript types: `AttendanceStreak`, `MemberAttendanceSummary`, `TrainerMemberAttendance`

### PHASE 5 — Owner Portal UI Improvements (`Attendance.tsx` + CSS)
- Remove UI assumptions around simulation
- Replace hardcoded `peakCapacity` with gym setting
- Add date-range picker (custom from/to)
- Add server-side pagination
- Show clear empty states when DB has no data
- Live Floor Panel enhancements (avatars, sticky panel)
- Export by custom date range
- Retention rate KPI; busiest hour callout; redesigned empty states

### PHASE 6 — Member Portal: My Attendance Page
- New route `/member/my-attendance`
- Sections: Streak banner; Monthly calendar; Recent visits table; Frequency chart; Self check-in button (if not checked-in today)
- Depends on Phase 3 member endpoints

### PHASE 7 — Trainer Portal: Member Attendance View
- Sections: My Members list (last visit, visit count, streak, absent alert); Drill-down calendar; Who’s inside now
- Depends on Phase 3 trainer endpoints

### PHASE 8 — Routing & Navigation
- `App.tsx`: Add `/member/my-attendance` route and navigation item
- Trainer nav: Add "Member Attendance" tab or route

### PHASE 9 — Equipment Reservation & Access Control (Foundation)
- API: `POST /api/equipment/{id}/reserve`, `GET /api/equipment/reservations`, `DELETE /api/equipment/reservations/{id}`
- Constraints: Membership tier access, capacity/time-slot rules
- Staff override paths and audit
- UI: Member equipment booking panel; Owner capacity settings

### PHASE 10 — Class Booking & Access Control
- API: Class capacity, waitlist, attendance marking (QR/self)
- UI: Member booking calendar; Trainer class attendance; Owner reports

### PHASE 11 — PT Session Access Control
- API: Trainer-member booking, limits per membership tier, completion logging
- UI: Trainer schedule; Member session history

### PHASE 12 — Billing/Payment Access Control
- Enforce role-scoped access to invoices, payments, and membership changes
- Align with RBAC audit to protect billing controllers

### PHASE 13 — Notifications & Alerts
- Absent alerts (7+ days) to assigned trainer
- Check-in confirmations to member
- Digest emails for owner (daily/weekly attendance summaries)

---

## ✅ Verification Plan

### Security & RBAC
- Verify `@PreAuthorize` on all controllers via automated scan
- Attempt role escalation and cross-gym data access; ensure denied

### Backend (curl tests)
- `POST /api/attendance/check-in` twice for same user/day → `409 CONFLICT`
- `PUT /api/attendance/check-out/{id}` with wrong user/role → `403 FORBIDDEN`
- `GET /api/attendance/stats` on empty DB → zeros, no simulation
- `GET /api/attendance/me/history` with MEMBER JWT → only self records
- Pagination: `GET /api/attendance/today?page=0&size=25` returns bounded list

### Frontend
- Owner: Analytics show real zeros when DB empty; pagination works
- Member: My Attendance shows streaks, calendar, self check-in
- Trainer: Sees only assigned members’ attendance

